<% content_for :title, "How it works · Handshake" %>
<h1>How it works</h1>
<section class="card stack">
  <h2>Start a chat</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><span>Pick where you are: scan a venue's table tent, type its zone and word, or use your rough area.</span></li>
    <li><span>Your screen shows a code like <strong class="nowrap">47-12-83</strong>. The first pair is the zone. It changes every minute.</span></li>
    <li><span>Say your codes to each other. Each of you types the other's. When both are in, a private chat opens.</span></li>
  </ol>
  <p class="muted small">Nobody can start a chat on their own: it takes both of you. A typo doesn't use up a code.</p>
</section>
<section class="card stack">
  <h2>Grow it into a group (up to 8)</h2>
  <p><strong>Add someone:</strong> in the chat menu, show them a one-time code and type theirs. Then everyone in the chat is asked.</p>
  <p><strong>Group handshake:</strong> all together? Open a 2-minute code anyone nearby can enter. They still need the group's yes.</p>
  <p class="muted small">By default everyone must agree. New people only see messages from after they join.</p>
</section>
<section class="card stack">
  <h2>Share more, one person at a time</h2>
  <p>In <em>People and reveals</em>, each step opens only when you've both chosen it: first name and photo, then socials, then phone number. Groups never see your details unless you share with each person.</p>
</section>
<section class="card stack">
  <h2>Leave any time</h2>
  <p>End a one-to-one chat and it disappears for both of you. Leave a group quietly. Chats vanish by themselves after 14 days unless everyone taps Extend.</p>
</section>
